  "limitations": [
    "CPU work uses approximate scalar OS25-derived timing with os30 cache sizes, not actual Vexii instruction timing.",
    "GPU raster/cache/mesh arbitration and 100MHz16-bit PSRAM controller/PHY timing are simulated using actual RTL.",
    "Frames start with an idle GPU and resident snapshot; carryover from prior frames, CPU/scanout SDRAM contention, audio/OS ISR costs and vblank are absent.",
    "The recorded CPU branch/control path is retained. Real ring-full, fence, and upload-busy waits stretch the producer; additional polling instruction costs are not executed.",
    "GPU unpublished command writes are packed at the end of the measured submission interval while preserving publish timing; reserve capacity is checked before CPU submission work.",
    "CPU non-framebuffer snapshots are installed after preceding fences and before submission. This validates these captured rendering outputs, not all CPU/GPU memory races.",
    "The render gate omits CPU framebuffer snapshots; full CPU framebuffer output has separate600-frame exact tests. Complete rendered color/depth match for every sample.",
    "All baseline scenes are pinned deployed13c8 app/currentMAC+CB4 core controls. Live81 reconstructs exactly one frame-start clear from independent command trace.",
    "Initial paced v1 serialized uploads after every word and overestimated extra upload delay. Only asynchronous issue/recorded busy-poll modelv3 and vectorsv2 are used here.",
    "Relative throughput estimates are scenario comparisons, not a measured Pocket FPS claim."
  ],
